    {
      "id": "p0209-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In English, Snowdrake's father has an unusual accent - he uses the word \"fathah\" instead of \"father\", for example. Toby explained in his translation notes that this character \"talks like a weird Jewish dad, in a stilted way\". This unique speech pattern suggests that the father might not be from the Hotland region to begin with.",
        "raw": "In English, Snowdrake's father has an unusual accent - he uses the word\n\"fathah\" instead of \"father\", for example. Toby explained in his translation\nnotes that this character \"talks like a weird Jewish dad, in a stilted way\". This\nunique speech pattern suggests that the father might not be from the Hotland\nregion to begin with.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08415906,
          0.28932143,
          0.68824656,
          0.37570714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0821176,
          0.28860714,
          0.70093421,
          0.37677857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          24,
          25,
          26,
          27,
          28
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "英语里，Snowdrake 的父亲口音很特别，例如他把 father（父亲）说成 fathah。Toby 在翻译说明中说，这个角色“像个古怪的犹太老爸，说话不太自然”。这种独特腔调暗示他可能原本并非热域居民。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.08829300886483449,
          0.28789286,
          0.7022611572139437,
          0.37927857
        ],
