      "review_issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0209-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "To retain this sense of \"outsider-ness\", the translator gave Snowdrake's father a thick Osaka accent. This makes perfect sense for two reasons: Osaka is the comedy capital of Japan, and Snowdrake already has an Osaka accent. The result: Snowdrake's father sounds like a .Japanese comedian who has passed on some of his traits and ambitions to his son.",
        "raw": "To retain this sense of \"outsider-ness\", the translator gave Snowdrake's father\na thick Osaka accent. This makes perfect sense for two reasons: Osaka is the\ncomedy capital of Japan, and Snowdrake already has an Osaka accent. The\nresult: Snowdrake's father sounds like a .Japanese comedian who has passed on\nsome of his traits and ambitions to his son.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08822156,
          0.39069286,
          0.69889275,
          0.47707857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0821176,
          0.38997857,
          0.70093421,
          0.47815
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          29,
          30,
          31,
          32,
          33
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "为保留这种“外来者”的感觉，译者让他讲浓重的大阪口音。这样做有两重道理：大阪是日本的喜剧之都，Snowdrake 本来也讲大阪口音。结果，父亲听起来像个日本喜剧演员，把自己的部分特点与志向传给了儿子。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
