    {
      "id": "p0209-b007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Manzai is a long-established form of Japanese stand-up comedy that traditionally features a team of two comedians. Much like the double-act comedy routines found in other countries, manzai usually involves one bokeh (\"funny man\") and one tsukkomi (\"straight man\") playing off of each other as ridiculous situations unfold.",
        "raw": "Manzai is a long-established form of Japanese stand-up comedy that\ntraditionally features a team of two comedians. Much like the double-act\ncomedy routines found in other countries, manzai usually involves one\nbokeh (\"funny man\") and one tsukkomi (\"straight man\") playing off of\neach other as ridiculous situations unfold.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.11664884,
          0.53912857,
          0.67588553,
          0.61788571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.1153219,
          0.53841429,
          0.67721248,
          0.61895714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          35,
          36,
          37,
          38,
          39
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Manzai（漫才）是日本历史悠久的舞台喜剧形式，传统上由两名演员搭档。与其他国家的双人喜剧相似，漫才通常由 bokeh（装傻逗趣者）与 tsukkomi（吐槽纠正者）相互配合，演出荒唐情境。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
